# =====================================================================
# Whoville-Client Playwright E2E Test Suite — Environment Variable Template
# =====================================================================
#
# This is a TEMPLATE file. It is safe to commit — it documents every
# environment variable the Playwright E2E suite reads, but contains no
# real secrets. To use:
#
#   1. Copy this file to `.env.e2e` in the repository root:
#          cp .env.e2e.example .env.e2e
#   2. Fill in real values for your local environment (especially the
#          E2E_TEST_USER_PASSWORD entry below).
#   3. Run any of the npm scripts:
#          npm run e2e:smoke
#          npm run e2e:crud
#          npm run e2e:integration
#
# IMPORTANT — DO NOT COMMIT `.env.e2e`:
# `.env.e2e` is listed in `.gitignore` per AAP §0.5.1.1 because it can
# contain real test-user passwords, API tokens, and connection strings.
# This template (`.env.e2e.example`) IS committed and is the source of
# truth for which variables exist; only the values are environment-specific.
#
# Loading mechanism (per AAP §0.6.1):
#   - `e2e/global-setup.ts` loads this file via `dotenv` at suite startup.
#   - Per-script invocations may load it explicitly via `dotenv-cli`, e.g.:
#         npx dotenv -e .env.e2e -- npx playwright test
#   - `playwright.config.ts` also calls `require('dotenv').config({ path: '.env.e2e' })`
#         at config-resolution time so `process.env.*` is populated before
#         Playwright reads `use.baseURL`, retries, workers, etc.
#
# CI integration:
#   - GitHub Actions: variables are injected from repository secrets, e.g.
#         env: { E2E_TEST_USER_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.E2E_TEST_USER_PASSWORD }} }
#   - Azure DevOps: variables are sourced from a variable group such as
#         `whoville-e2e-secrets` linked to each pipeline.
#   - In CI, `.env.e2e` is NOT created on disk; values are passed as real
#         process environment variables and consumed identically by `dotenv`.
#
# References:
#   - AAP §0.5.1.1 — file purpose and required variable list
#   - AAP §0.6.1   — `dotenv` and `dotenv-cli` consumption
#   - AAP §0.9.1   — "Environment setup requirements for tests" table
#   - e2e/README.md — full developer onboarding walkthrough
#
# =====================================================================


# =====================================================================
# === Required Variables ===
# =====================================================================
# These three variables MUST be set (or left at their committed defaults)
# for any tier of the suite to execute successfully. The defaults shown
# work out-of-the-box for local development against the standard Angular
# CLI dev server (`ng serve` on port 4200).

# E2E_BASE_URL — The base URL of the running Whoville-Client Angular dev/staging server.
# Default: http://localhost:4200 (Angular CLI default port for `ng serve`).
# Consumed by: playwright.config.ts (use.baseURL) and e2e/global-setup.ts.
E2E_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4200

# E2E_API_MODE — Controls whether API calls are mocked or routed to a live backend.
# Allowed values: 'mock' (default) | 'live'
# When 'mock': page.route('**/api/**', ...) interceptors are registered.
# When 'live': all interceptors are bypassed; suite calls real backend at $E2E_BASE_URL.
# Consumed by: e2e/fixtures/mock-api.fixture.ts.
E2E_API_MODE=mock

# MOCK_API — Boolean toggle that complements E2E_API_MODE for legacy compatibility.
# Allowed values: 'true' (default) | 'false'
# When 'true' AND E2E_API_MODE='mock': mock fixture is active (the canonical default).
# When 'false' AND E2E_API_MODE='live': interceptors disabled (live-backend mode).
# Keep aligned with E2E_API_MODE: mock+true OR live+false.
# Consumed by: e2e/global-setup.ts.
MOCK_API=true


# =====================================================================
# === Authentication ===
# =====================================================================
# Credentials used by global-setup.ts (and the standalone
# e2e/scripts/generate-storage-states.ts script) to perform a one-time
# login per role and persist the resulting cookies + localStorage as
# `e2e/storage-states/<role>.json`. All test workers reuse those files
# so the login flow runs at most once per worker per suite, not on every
# test (per AAP §0.4.4 "Worker-scoped storage state").

# E2E_TEST_USER_USERNAME — Username used by global-setup.ts to generate the
# canonical authenticated storageState file (e2e/storage-states/canonical-user.json).
# In CI, this comes from a repository secret (e.g., GitHub Actions secret or Azure DevOps variable group).
E2E_TEST_USER_USERNAME=test.user@whoville.example.internal

# E2E_TEST_USER_PASSWORD — Password matching the username above.
# NEVER commit a real password to this template file or to .env.e2e committed to source control.
# In CI, this MUST come from a secret store; never hard-code in workflow YAML.
E2E_TEST_USER_PASSWORD=replace-with-real-password

# Optional per-role credentials (used when running RBAC denial tests in Tier 3):
# Uncomment and populate any role you wish to exercise. Each role gets its
# own storageState file (e.g., e2e/storage-states/admin.json) and is
# consumed by tests via the `adminPage`, `viewerPage`, `restrictedPage`
# fixture overrides defined in e2e/fixtures/auth.fixture.ts.
# E2E_ADMIN_USER_USERNAME=
# E2E_ADMIN_USER_PASSWORD=
# E2E_VIEWER_USER_USERNAME=
# E2E_VIEWER_USER_PASSWORD=
# E2E_RESTRICTED_USER_USERNAME=
# E2E_RESTRICTED_USER_PASSWORD=


# =====================================================================
# === Reporting & CI ===
# =====================================================================
# These variables tune the reporter pipeline, retry/worker policy, and
# CI-specific behaviors (e.g., disabling auto-open of the HTML report).
# Defaults below match the values consumed by `playwright.config.ts`.

# CI — Set to 'true' on CI runners; affects retry policy, worker count, and HTML report auto-open behavior.
# Default in playwright.config.ts: process.env.CI is checked at config-resolution time.
# When set to ANY non-empty value (including 'false', '0', etc.):
#     retries=2, workers='50%', forbidOnly=true, reporter includes 'github' annotations.
# When unset (or commented out):
#     retries=0, workers=undefined (Playwright auto-detects), HTML report opens on failure.
# Note: playwright.config.ts uses `!!process.env.CI`, so the JavaScript truthiness rule
# applies — the literal string 'false' is truthy. To force local mode after copying this
# template, COMMENT OUT or DELETE the CI line below; do not rely on CI=false to disable it.
# Most CI providers (GitHub Actions, Azure DevOps, GitLab, CircleCI) set CI=true automatically.
CI=false

# PLAYWRIGHT_HTML_REPORT — Output directory for the HTML report (relative to repo root).
# Default: playwright-report/ (matches .gitignore entry).
# Consumed by: playwright.config.ts (reporter html outputFolder) and
# e2e/scripts/coverage-report.ts (writes e2e-coverage.html alongside).
PLAYWRIGHT_HTML_REPORT=playwright-report

# PLAYWRIGHT_JUNIT_OUTPUT_NAME — Output file path for JUnit XML report.
# Default: test-results/junit.xml (matches .gitignore entry).
# Consumed by: playwright.config.ts (reporter junit outputFile).
# CI systems (Azure DevOps, GitHub Actions test-reporter actions) ingest
# this file to render per-test status in the pipeline UI.
PLAYWRIGHT_JUNIT_OUTPUT_NAME=test-results/junit.xml


# =====================================================================
# === Optional / Advanced ===
# =====================================================================
# These variables are commented out by default; uncomment only when you
# need to override the in-repo Playwright defaults. Each entry documents
# its allowed values and the default that takes effect when unset.

# PWDEBUG — When set to '1', launches Playwright Inspector for step-by-step debugging.
# Set this in your shell when running `npm run e2e:debug`.
# Allowed values: '1' (Inspector on) | '' (default, Inspector off) | 'console' (debug via console only)
# The npm script `e2e:debug` already sets this via cross-env, so you only
# need to export it manually if invoking `playwright test` directly.
# PWDEBUG=1

# PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH — Override location of installed browser binaries.
# Useful in containerized CI to share binaries across pipeline jobs.
# Default: ~/.cache/ms-playwright/ on Linux/macOS.
# Set to '0' to install browsers inside node_modules/playwright-core/.local-browsers/
# (useful for reproducible per-project installs when caching node_modules).
# PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=/path/to/browsers

# E2E_RETRY_COUNT — Override retry count globally; takes precedence over project config.
# Allowed values: 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 (integer)
# Default per playwright.config.ts: 0 locally, 2 in CI (smoke/crud=1, integration=2).
# Use sparingly — habitual retries mask flake; fix the underlying cause instead.
# E2E_RETRY_COUNT=2

# E2E_WORKERS — Override worker count globally; takes precedence over project config.
# Examples: '50%' (default in CI), '100%' (default locally), or a fixed integer like '4'.
# Default per playwright.config.ts: '50%' in CI, undefined (auto) locally.
# Set to '1' to force serial execution when debugging order-dependent flakes.
# E2E_WORKERS=50%

# E2E_TRACE — Override trace mode. Allowed: 'on', 'off', 'on-first-retry' (default), 'retain-on-failure'.
# Default per playwright.config.ts: 'on-first-retry' (trace captured only when a test retries).
# Set 'on' for migration-era debugging where every test run benefits from a trace.
# Set 'retain-on-failure' to keep traces only for failing tests (saves disk in CI).
# E2E_TRACE=on-first-retry


# =====================================================================
# === Live API Mode (only when E2E_API_MODE=live) ===
# =====================================================================
# These variables are inert when E2E_API_MODE=mock (the default). When
# you flip E2E_API_MODE=live for a periodic integration validation run
# (typically the nightly `e2e-live-api-nightly.yml` workflow per AAP
# §0.5.1.14), uncomment and populate the entries below.

# When running against a real backend instead of mocks, point E2E_BASE_URL at the
# live Whoville-Client deployment (e.g., staging) and configure VPN/connectivity.
# This OVERRIDES the localhost default at the top of this file.
# E2E_BASE_URL=https://staging.whoville.example.internal

# Optional API token override (overrides login flow if set):
# When provided, e2e/global-setup.ts skips the username/password login flow
# and writes the token directly into the storageState localStorage entry.
# Useful for service-account-driven CI runs against staging.
# E2E_API_TOKEN=

# Per AAP §0.4.4 "Live-mode database hygiene": entities created in live mode
# use the prefix 'e2e-test-' so the nightly cleanup workflow can identify and remove them.
# Override this prefix only if a different value is required by environment policy
# (e.g., a per-team prefix to support concurrent test runs in shared staging).
# E2E_TEST_DATA_PREFIX=e2e-test-


# =====================================================================
# References:
# =====================================================================
# Where each variable is consumed in the codebase. Use this map to trace
# any variable back to the file(s) that read it, in support of code review,
# refactoring, and migration auditing.
#
# - playwright.config.ts        — reads E2E_BASE_URL, CI, PLAYWRIGHT_HTML_REPORT
# - e2e/global-setup.ts         — reads E2E_API_MODE, E2E_TEST_USER_*, MOCK_API
# - e2e/fixtures/mock-api.fixture.ts  — reads MOCK_API, E2E_API_MODE
# - e2e/scripts/generate-storage-states.ts — reads E2E_TEST_USER_USERNAME, E2E_TEST_USER_PASSWORD
# - e2e/scripts/coverage-report.ts        — reads PLAYWRIGHT_HTML_REPORT
# =====================================================================
